{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543056-so-i-d-like-to-have-some-opinions-if-possible-because-this-is-crazy","id":1543056,"title":"So, I'd like to have some opinions, if possible, because this is crazy...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-03T05:54:29-07:00","id":1543056,"title":"So, I'd like to have some opinions, if possible, because this is crazy...","content":"On one of my chronicles of Sorcere's Crusade, a mage is in love a vampire lady. He adores her, but he also wants to have an heir and she can't possibly give him one (for obvious reasons, if I'm not mistaken there's only a way for a vampire to have a baby &quot;normally&quot; that is with the merit Blasphemous pact). So, the player came to me with a plan to collect what would be called nowadays &quot;his dna&quot; and hers and somehow insert their &quot;combined biological material&quot; in another woman to have their children.<br /> <br /> I mean it's absolutely crazy, but as much as I like crazy ideas, I told him no at first and then told him I would consult with other experiencd ST like myself to see if anyone would have a favourable opinion to this crazy idea. As much as I find the idea interesting in a crazy way, I don't see how it would fit to any paradigm of the 16th century (where the story takes place). <br /> <br /> What do you people think about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-03T07:53:19-07:00","id":1543058,"title":"","content":"IF you want to give them this, then I would use the Thaumaturgy ritual called:<br /> <br /> <b><b>Domino of Life (</b></b>Guide to the Sabbat pg. 119, Players Guide to the Sabbat pg. 116 or Vampire: The Dark Ages 20th Anniversary Edition pg. 303)<br /> <br /> A vampire wanting or needing to simulate a human characteristic can do so once Domino of Life is cast. For one entire night, the vampire can eat, breathe, maintain a normal body temperature, assume a human flesh tone, <b>or display some other single trait of humankind</b> she desires. Note that only one trait can be replicated in this fashion. The vampire must have a vial of fresh human blood on his person to maintain this ritual.<br /> <br /> In this case the trait would be:<i> the ability too bear a child</i><br /> One day - but that could be with Mage magic extended to last 9 months even...<br /> Or any Mage (or True Brujah Temporis...) shenanigans<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-03T08:24:20-07:00","id":1543059,"title":"","content":"This is quite possible in the paradigm of the time. While DNA was not known, Aristotle posited that a male's seed mixed with a sort of substrate secreted by a female to produce offspring. For males, that was semen, for females, menses. So as an alternative to using time magic, if his lover can have a period, he could do a ritual to mix those two substances and implant it in a surrogate mother. That's Life 5, if he doesn't have to filter out vitae. But he may have to prevent the surrogate mother from influencing the child. At least during later periods it was believed the mother's thoughts and feelings during pregnancy could influence the child. So you'd need a Life 4/Mind 1 effect to block out that influence, and possibly Mind 3 to connect his lover to the child.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-03T10:02:31-07:00","id":1543064,"title":"","content":"What you are describing is a <b>homunculus</b>, a sort of mainstay of alchemy for several hundred years. The term was first used by the Swiss philosopher, physician, and alchemist Paracelsus in his 1537 work <i>De Natura Rerum</i>, but the concept probably predates that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That the sperm of a man be putrefied by itself in a sealed cucurbit for forty days with the highest degree of putrefaction in a horse's womb [&quot;<i>venter equinus</i>&quot;, meaning &quot;warm, fermenting horse dung&quot;], or at least so long that it comes to life and moves itself, and stirs, which is easily observed. After this time, it will look somewhat like a man, but transparent, without a body. If, after this, it be fed wisely with the Arcanum of human blood, and be nourished for up to forty weeks, and be kept in the even heat of the horse's womb, a living human child grows therefrom, with all its members like another child, which is born of a woman, but much smaller. </div> </div> </div>In this case, you would probably use the vampire's blood, and potentially end up with a dhampir like what is described in Vampire the Masquerade's Time of Thin Blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-03T15:59:23-07:00","id":1543070,"title":"","content":"Theories about what substances and conditions produces babies predate Aristotle, as do ideas on how to produces \u201cartificial\u201d humans. That\u2019s definitely something that would exist at the time and actually far earlier, regardless of modern notions about DNA.<br /> <br /> What he needs is a thesis on how to produce a new human being through magical means, and a thesis on how to capture the essence of the mother that would normally be passed through a pregnancy. None of those is out of place at the time.<br /> <br /> But above that, I\u2019m actually curious about why you put such a high bar for this to be done? It is still Mage: pushing the envelop is par of the course for the game, and operating under personal beliefs that go beyond the thoughts of your time. I fail to see any reason to deny this to your PC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-03T17:26:57-07:00","id":1543071,"title":"","content":"Not only would the male mortal's semen need to fertilize the female vampire's egg, they would need to be able to remove it from the vampire and implant it within another living woman's uterus. For me, there are just too many steps, and those steps have some unknowns that would need to be settled or risks eliminated before it could work. So rather than bother, I'd just say &quot;no&quot; were I the ST.<br /> <br /> First, neither male or female vampires have any living sperm or eggs. They would have died when they died/became vampires. Woman never create new eggs (ok, there is some evidence this may not be true, but it's really speculation). They just have those that they are already born with. Men do create new sperm, but sperm take 50-60 days to develop. So I don't think Domino of Life would work in that regard as it takes effect for only one day. I understand some STs might want to handwave that, but I think that is a very different situation than saying you can emulate eating, breathing, live flesh tone, etc. which seems like a weaker version of vampires on the path of humanity engaging in the Blush of Life.<br /> <br /> Second, even if you assume the vampire's existing sperm or eggs can be used, won't there be a significant chance that it's so damaged from the trauma of being undead that either it is useless or will result in some terrible defect? If living women who wait too long to have children end up not becoming pregnant even though they still have eggs, what must it be like for (dead) eggs stuck in a vampire's dead body?<br /> <br /> Third, how are you going to make sure the egg gets fertilized? In actual IVF procedure a doctor takes multiple eggs in order to make sure that even one can become fertilized. And fertilization is not guaranteed even with normal sex. There is a good chance this will fail even if you allow it.<br /> <br /> Fourth, how are you going to retrieve the fertilized egg (or even a theoretically healthy but unfertilized egg for later fertilization) without damaging it? Such surgeries would be common place and safely and routinely done by trained medical professionals with lots of modern equipment. How can this be done in the era of the Sorcerer's Crusade even assuming the vampire cannot be harmed during the process.<br /> <br /> Fifth, how are you going to do the embryo transfer? Again, this requires a degree or medical knowledge, training, and equipment that I do not believe exists in the era of the Sorcerer's Crusade. And unlike concerns about the vampire's health that you can dismiss, this procedure could very well kill the surrogate.<br /> <br /> Some STs can always come up with excuses for these objections, but for me there are just too many unknowns and risks. Far simpler to just not allow it. Even if the chronicle took place in the modern day when some of these objections could not apply, I still think there's some fundamentally wrong things with it to work.<br /> <br /> However, per <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a>, a Mage could create some kind of homonculus from a combination of the man's sperm and the vampire's vitae. That would be appropriate for the era of the Sorcerer's Crusade. However, I would not make the issue of such a blasphemous and horrific union a real human child, but some kind of monster or abomination. Maybe the child looks human, but there would be something wrong with it. This is the origin of things like Widderslainte.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=K7AKLKQqfj4\" data-code=\"K7AKLKQqfj4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/K7AKLKQqfj4/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-AUBlW5EWnI\" data-code=\"-AUBlW5EWnI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/-AUBlW5EWnI/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XgRwQl5i_5o\" data-code=\"XgRwQl5i_5o\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/XgRwQl5i_5o/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> So unlike some of the other posters here, I wouldn't handwave it just because it's Mage. I may not be in the majority.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-03T18:22:44-07:00","id":1543074,"title":"","content":"I think whether or not this turns out well should be tied to the morality of the mage and the vampire. If the vampire is trying to be a good person (in other words, has high Humanity), their love is true and genuine, the surrogate undergoes the procedure consensually and is on good terms with the mage and the vampire, and the mage uses their power for good deeds, I think it's entirely appropriate to treat this as not blasphemous and horrific at all. The process of loving and raising a child, a true <i>mortal</i> child, could pull the vampire closer to mortal virtues. If this is the case, the child should be a normal child... or maybe even just a little bit blessed.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if the vampire is low Humanity, their love is poison, they force the surrogate into it, and the mage abuses his power, the product of their union should be appropriately warped and evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-03T18:28:33-07:00","id":1543075,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I mean, even with the homunculus idea, what you end up with isn't human. At best it is a simulacrum that tries to mimic humans and always falls short. At worst it might end up as a monstrous sociopath combining the worst aspects of Frankenstein, The Bad Seed, and The Midwich Cuckoos. I suggested making it a (pseudo)dhampir simply because of the Vampire aspect.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-03T19:06:48-07:00","id":1543076,"title":"","content":"Wow! Thanks very much everyone for adding so much to the discussion, I'll try to comment on every responde so far (as much as I can, because as a college student I'm quite tired and need to go to bed soon, but I'll do my best).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><b>Domino of Life (</b></b>Guide to the Sabbat pg. 119, Players Guide to the Sabbat pg. 116 or Vampire: The Dark Ages 20th Anniversary Edition pg. 303) </div> </div> </div>To be honest I didn't even think about this ritual, likely because it has a short duration for the whole thing, that's why I mentioned the only thing I know that could totally circumvent it that was the Blasphmous pact merit. In any case, it would be somewhat simple to increase the duration if that was the only problem. My main concern was paradigm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While DNA was not known, Aristotle posited that a male's seed mixed with a sort of substrate secreted by a female to produce offspring. </div> </div> </div>That's a very interesting thing you said, food for thought indeed, with this in mind and a pure mechanical mindset it should be no problem at all to make it happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What you are describing is a <b>homunculus</b>, a sort of mainstay of alchemy for several hundred years. The term was first used by the Swiss philosopher, physician, and alchemist Paracelsus in his 1537 work <i>De Natura Rerum</i>, but the concept probably predates that.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Another very interesting responde that made me really see the whole thig through different lenses<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What he needs is a thesis on how to produce a new human being through magical means, and a thesis on how to capture the essence of the mother that would normally be passed through a pregnancy </div> </div> </div>That was my main concern all along and the main reason I said &quot;no&quot; at first, because as I see it, that is the hardest part of the whole thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I fail to see any reason to deny this to your PC </div> </div> </div>Again, the main reason is that I couldn't see or create a good thery/thesis for the feat. The ideas people gave me here made me reevaluate the whole thing, I'm now thinking if I can come up with a good thesis for that, even though <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> gave quite a long argument against it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543056-so-i-d-like-to-have-some-opinions-if-possible-because-this-is-crazy?p=1543075#post1543075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. I mean, even with the homunculus idea, what you end up with isn't human. At best it is a simulacrum that tries to mimic humans and always falls short. At worst it might end up as a monstrous sociopath combining the worst aspects of Frankenstein, The Bad Seed, and The Midwich Cuckoos. I suggested making it a (pseudo)dhampir simply because of the Vampire aspect.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's a good opportunity to pull the Samuel Haight card and make it an awakened dhampir child hahaha","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-03T22:59:24-07:00","id":1543086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543056-so-i-d-like-to-have-some-opinions-if-possible-because-this-is-crazy?p=1543071#post1543071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, there are just too many steps, and those steps have some unknowns that would need to be settled or risks eliminated before it could work. So rather than bother, I'd just say &quot;no&quot; were I the ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>I partially disagree.<br /> <br /> All your considerations are only relevant from a modern perspective. Which may well be how the WoD really works, but is not how Awakened Magic works. As long as the PC has enough Spheres to make it work, they only need a theory, not to be right about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543056-so-i-d-like-to-have-some-opinions-if-possible-because-this-is-crazy?p=1543071#post1543071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I would not make the issue of such a blasphemous and horrific union a real human child, but some kind of monster or abomination.</div> </div> </div> </div>That, I somewhat agree. The whole ordeal working doesn\u2019t necessarily means a normal, human child being born.<br /> <br /> But I would let the precise way they\u2019re strange in the air, as to adapt to the story as it unfolds. I find the idea of defaulting to horror just because a vampire is involved.. unnerving. But sure, if it works to the story, then so be it.<br /> <br /> I think it would be something at least a bit inhuman anyway, and possibly terribly monstrous. The idea of a Dhampir is a good start, and sure, maybe it\u2019s a Widderslainte.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T03:57:37-07:00","id":1543090,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem is the main question of Alarune (a German novel made into several silent films). Was the young woman evil because of her blasphemous origin, the degenerate nature of her bio parents, or the simple fact that the man who raised her was an emotionally closed off pseudo intellectual who treated her as an experiment rather than a child? <br /> <br /> You would need to figure out what's important in your campaign. Remember Frankenstien's creature and Alarune were abused by those that had the responsibility to raise them. Beatrice Rappancini (also a form of the Panadora myth) was also abused by her father, but he also dearly loved her. Unlike the nameless creature and Alarune she could be kind and loving. <br /> <br /> The homuculus this Mage and Vampire create will be most deeply influenced by who the people who raise him are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T08:39:45-07:00","id":1543149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543056-so-i-d-like-to-have-some-opinions-if-possible-because-this-is-crazy?p=1543090#post1543090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the problem is the main question of Alarune (a German novel made into several silent films). Was the young woman evil because of her blasphemous origin, the degenerate nature of her bio parents, or the simple fact that the man who raised her was an emotionally closed off pseudo intellectual who treated her as an experiment rather than a child?<br /> <br /> You would need to figure out what's important in your campaign. Remember Frankenstien's creature and Alarune were abused by those that had the responsibility to raise them. Beatrice Rappancini (also a form of the Panadora myth) was also abused by her father, but he also dearly loved her. Unlike the nameless creature and Alarune she could be kind and loving.<br /> <br /> The homuculus this Mage and Vampire create will be most deeply influenced by who the people who raise him are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly agree that it should be mehr about who raised him than anything else.<br /> That book seems like a very interesting reading, thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T09:54:06-07:00","id":1543151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543056-so-i-d-like-to-have-some-opinions-if-possible-because-this-is-crazy?p=1543149#post1543149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I certainly agree that it should be mehr about who raised him than anything else.<br /> That book seems like a very interesting reading, thank you!</div> </div> </div> </div>Trust me the various films are more approachable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T10:50:24-07:00","id":1543153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543056-so-i-d-like-to-have-some-opinions-if-possible-because-this-is-crazy?p=1543151#post1543151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Trust me the various films are more approachable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, I'll try to watch one of them, do you have any suggestion?<br /> <br /> And when I say that the way the child was reised should be more important, I also ackowledge the fact that &quot;something strange&quot; should be present, perhaps something similar to a psychopath, that is a thing one cannot change, at least according to most theories on the subject, it's something one is born with. In any case, the child can learn to control such impulses and that can become a very interesting story in itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T17:52:01-07:00","id":1543175,"title":"","content":"Find what is available to you. The silents were more faithful to the book, the newer ones are tawdry at the expense of theme and story.<br /> <br /> I can't give you more help than that because these films are only irregularly available in the USA or English speaking countries generally.<br /> <br /> It might be useful to know that Alarune means Mandrake. Mandrakes were often used to make homunculi. The aspect of the legendary Mandrakes refered to in the story is the association between the gallows and Mandrakes. When men are hanged by the neck until dead, in the death process most males ejaculate. It's assumed to be caused by chaos in the dying brain. When the seminal fluid of dying men is spilled on the ground Mandrakes are supposed to take root.<br /> <br /> In the story the seminal fluid of a dying man is collected and used to impregnate a prostitute. Alarune is thus a homuculus born from death.<br /> <br /> In most forms of the story she seems to have some kind of unconscious influence on fate, bringing riches or ruin. She also seemed to have the ability to manipulate people's appetites for sex and adventure and to cloud their judgment. Again she seems to have no conscious control of this power.<br /> <br /> Does any of that help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 10-05-2024, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T23:52:23-07:00","id":1543185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543056-so-i-d-like-to-have-some-opinions-if-possible-because-this-is-crazy?p=1543175#post1543175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Find what is available to you. The silents were more faithful to the book, the newer ones are tawdry at the expense of theme and story.<br /> <br /> I can't give you more help than that because these films are only irregularly available in the USA or English speaking countries generally.<br /> <br /> It might be useful to know that Alarune means Mandrake. Mandrakes were often used to make homunculi. The aspect of the legendary Mandrakes refered to in the story is the association between the gallows and Mandrakes. When men are hanged by the neck until dead, in the death process most males ejaculate. It's assumed to be caused by chaos in the dying brain. When the seminal fluid of dying men is spilled on the ground Mandrakes are supposed to take root.<br /> <br /> In the story the seminal fluid of a dying man is collected and used to impregnate a prostitute. Alarune is thus a homuculus born from death.<br /> <br /> In most forms of the story she seems to have some kind of unconscious influence on fate, bringing riches or ruin. She also seemed to have the ability to manipulate people's appetites for sex and adventure and to cloud their judgment. Again she seems to have no conscious control of this power.<br /> <br /> Does any of that help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly that does help! Thank you very much! I'll see if I can find it. That might give me some ideas for this future story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T05:00:28-07:00","id":1543195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543056-so-i-d-like-to-have-some-opinions-if-possible-because-this-is-crazy?p=1543071#post1543071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not only would the male mortal's semen need to fertilize the female vampire's egg, they would need to be able to remove it from the vampire and implant it within another living woman's uterus. For me, there are just too many steps, and those steps have some unknowns that would need to be settled or risks eliminated before it could work. So rather than bother, I'd just say &quot;no&quot; were I the ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sea man? Eggs? What in the name of Promethean nonsense propaganda are you talking about here? Everybody knows that babies are created by combining the right humours fluids, it is a combination of the sperm that is part of the fire humors of the body of the man and the water humours of the mother!<br /> <br /> Or, perhaps it is a combination of spirit essences under the wheel of fate.<br /> <br /> Remember, this is Mage we are talking about. &quot;Scientific facts&quot; is just a bunch of bullshittery used for propaganda purposes.<br /> <br /> And, even if &quot;sperm&quot; and &quot;eggs&quot; are real in the game's universe (debatable), you can still create them using Life 5 regardless. Heck, with Life 5 Spirit 5 you can even make a freaking SPIRIT get pregnant, so why not a vampire.<br /> <br /> With Life 5 Matter 5 and enough successes, you could make a female vampire get pregnant and carry out the pregnancy to terms, no need for a surrogate mother at all.<br /> <br /> That would be seem as some sort of satanic necromantic shit at the time by anyone however, so beware...<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T05:22:28-07:00","id":1543197,"title":"","content":"About the whole &quot;the child should be monstrous&quot;, there's no real need for that. Technocrats create real and new humans inside of tubes, out of nothing, who are fully functional and well adjust. There are special traits for these clones, sure, but that's because the techies have the annoying tendency to want to &quot;augment&quot; their vat lab boys.<br /> <br /> You are however free to add some inhuman traits to the process, particularly if the player wants to induce some specific traits, or small details (possibly cosmetic ones) due to resonance, or bigger ones if there's Paradox involved.<br /> <br /> Vampiric resonance is massive, but any negatives can be mitigated with enough successes, besides, if the vamp-lady has high humanity and their love is true, it could actually create a child with a &quot;blessed aura&quot; rather than something monstrous and cursed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T05:26:45-07:00","id":1543198,"title":"","content":"And as for the Paradigm side of things rather than the game mechanic side, that part has been well explained by others, such as the Homunculi theories for instance. That one would be well fit for either hermetics, prometheans and a few other groups. For choristers, that would probably be a blasphemy however - still doable, but...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T15:10:20-07:00","id":1543219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543056-so-i-d-like-to-have-some-opinions-if-possible-because-this-is-crazy?p=1543195#post1543195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember, this is Mage we are talking about. &quot;Scientific facts&quot; is just a bunch of bullshittery used for propaganda purposes.\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually disagree with you here. Even in Mage, phenomenon exists independently of any kind of consensual reality or Mage paradigm. The sun rises in the east and sets in the west. The solar and lunar cycles are known. Things thrown up in the air eventually come down. What Mages do as will workers is figure out why these phenomenon happen and duplicate them. When Mages try to break fundamental phenomenen like this, the result is always some horrible Paradox backlash or worse.<br /> <br /> You can argue all you want about semantics, but it would not be hard to articulate my interpretation in whatever terminology the people of the 17th century would use. Dead women did not give birth to children even back then. If they ever did, people would likely interpret any issue as some kind of monster.<br /> <br /> Actual Parcelsian homunculi are not real human beings. They are artificial, miniature, humanlike creatures. They are no more human than, say, the golem of Prague. In Mage terms they are best emulated as &quot;Familiars&quot;. The creation of a familiar is not the same as giving birth to an actual new human being.<br /> <br /> So while human conception does remain a mystery during this time, it doesn't mean &quot;facts&quot; are bullshit. The idea that facts are bullshit is what leads to Mages entering quiet, becoming Marauders, and being shunt away from reality.<br /> <br /> Life 5 is powerful, but it doesn't mean it allow you to create life from nothing. You still need foci, an appropriate paradigm, a paradigm that is accepted by the Sleepers to work, and lots of other things and still hope that Paradox doesn't wipe it out. If simply having a &quot;5&quot; in the appropriate spheres means you can do anything, then the Ascension War would either have been won thousands of years ago or the entire Pattern have been shredded as rival Mages with such powers create so many contradictions everything falls apart.<br /> <br /> It is the job of the ST to portray a coherent setting. As part of this it is also important to remember what the genre conventions of your setting are. Things that make sense in a completely, magical fantasy world don't make sense in a science fiction setting. Space opera operates under different tropes than hard science fiction. A D&amp;D style high fantasy setting is different than a sword &amp; sorcery genre. Mage is not in its own world, it is part of the World of Darkness which is rooted in the gothic tradition. Thus it is not a world where man intervening in things best left to god - and the creation of life is foremost of that - leads to good things. And creating a simulacrum of life is at or past the line of blasphemy. Certainly in the era of the Sorcerer's Crusade it is so. You can run Mage as a gonzo setting with little limitations set on the basic game mechanics, but the end result is not the World of Darkness but an entirely different kind of setting.<br /> <br /> The stories told in the gothic tradition about mankind trying to create their own new kind of life independent of a fertile living men and women always have the end result be bad. That's true whether it is Mary Shelly's Frankenstein, Hanns Heinz Ewer's Alraune, Arthur Machen's Great God Pan, or many other stories. The birth of unnatural &quot;children&quot; never ends well. You may prefer other inspirations.<br /> <br /> I certainly understand that some Mage players and STs prefer a setting whose interpretation is different than mine. My preferences are obviously different, but are not any less &quot;correct&quot; than yours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T20:05:08-07:00","id":1543242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543056-so-i-d-like-to-have-some-opinions-if-possible-because-this-is-crazy?p=1543219#post1543219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can argue all you want about semantics, but it would not be hard to articulate my interpretation in whatever terminology the people of the 17th century would use. Dead women did not give birth to children even back then. If they ever did, people would likely interpret any issue as some kind of monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just about this part: folklore does have quite a few stories about people born through magical means, and that does include dead parents. While it is usually an undead father (Dhampyr is an actual legend about this), the amount of legends linking undead women to pregnant women does mean this isn\u2019t too out-of-theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T22:30:45-07:00","id":1543252,"title":"","content":"Hey, I just met you<br /> And this is crazy<br /> But here's my vitae<br /> So child, maybe?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(I'm not apologizing, except for being late to think of it.)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T14:18:58-07:00","id":1543635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543056-so-i-d-like-to-have-some-opinions-if-possible-because-this-is-crazy?p=1543242#post1543242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just about this part: folklore does have quite a few stories about people born through magical means, and that does include dead parents. While it is usually an undead father (Dhampyr is an actual legend about this), the amount of legends linking undead women to pregnant women does mean this isn\u2019t too out-of-theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I totally agree with you here and this alone is already enough reason and I'm going to allow him to go ahead with his plan, now that I think about it again, it's a very interesting tale to explore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}